\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The auditor's confound-agnostic detect$\rightarrow $\allowbreak  localize$\rightarrow $\allowbreak  name$\rightarrow $\allowbreak  mitigate loop. Attribution (Grad-CAM) and mitigation (DFR) operate on a generic confound description --- a region box, or a \texttt  {(confound, label)} column pair --- and run unmodified across the synthetic tag, the real chest tube, and the cross-site case. The naming stage is isolated behind a \texttt  {crops/ + manifest.json} $\rightarrow $ \texttt  {predictions.jsonl} file contract: it is the only component with an external, rate-limited dependency, and no method in the mitigation path imports it, so the mitigation result is naming-independent by construction, not merely by claim.}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:architecture}{{1}{5}{}{figure.1}{}}
